  <!-- llms.txt -->
  <section id="llms-txt">
    <h2>📄 llms.txt: The New robots.txt for AI Crawlers</h2>

    <div class="highlight-box">
      <h4>📅 What is it?</h4>
      <p><strong>llms.txt</strong> is a proposed (and rapidly adopted) standard introduced by Jeremy Howard (Answer.AI) in 2024. It's a plain-text or markdown file at <code>yourdomain.com/llms.txt</code> that tells LLM crawlers and agents the "best entry points" to your site — distilled summaries of your most important content, in a format optimized for AI consumption.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:10px"><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://llmstxt.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">llmstxt.org — the proposal</a></p>
    </div>

    <h3>How is it different from robots.txt and sitemap.xml?</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>File</th>
          <th>Audience</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>robots.txt</code></td>
          <td>Search engine crawlers (Googlebot, Bingbot)</td>
          <td>Tell bots what NOT to crawl</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>sitemap.xml</code></td>
          <td>Search engine crawlers</td>
          <td>List of all crawlable URLs</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>llms.txt</code></td>
          <td>LLM agents (ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity)</td>
          <td>Curated, summarized entry points + key facts about your site</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Minimum viable llms.txt</h3>
    <pre><code># Waseem's SEO Guide

> A free, beginner-to-advanced course on SEO and Generative Engine
> Optimization (GEO). Built by Waseem, an English teacher and
> full-stack developer based in Haifa, Israel.

## Core curriculum

- [Level 1 — SEO Basics](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/level1/):
  Title tags, H1, links, alt text, schema markup.
- [Level 2 — Technical SEO](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/level2/):
  robots.txt, sitemaps, status codes, INP (2024), LCP, CLS.
- [Level 3 — Advanced GEO](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/level3/):
  AI Overviews, schema for trust, entity optimization, E-E-A-T.
- [Level 4 — Authority &amp; Channels](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/level4/):
  Backlinks, GBP, reviews, video SEO, social.

## Hands-on labs

- [Title Tag SERP Preview](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/labs/title-tag-tester/)
- [Schema Validator](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/labs/schema-validator/)
- [robots.txt Simulator](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/labs/robots-txt-simulator/)
- [Meta Tag Generator](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/labs/meta-tag-generator/)
- [Heading Structure Analyzer](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/labs/heading-analyzer/)

## Optional

- [Sources &amp; citations](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/sources/)
- [Glossary](https://ward3107.github.io/seo-guide-astro/glossary/)
</code></pre>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <h4>✅ Best practices</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep it under 100KB.</li>
        <li>Use markdown headings and links — LLMs already parse this perfectly.</li>
        <li>Lead with a 1–2 sentence "what this site is" summary in blockquote.</li>
        <li>Group sections by purpose (curriculum, tools, references).</li>
        <li>Place it at the root: <code>https://yourdomain.com/llms.txt</code>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="key-takeaway-box">
      <h4>🎯 Key Takeaway</h4>
      <p>llms.txt is the AI-era equivalent of an XML sitemap, but human-readable and summary-first. It's been adopted by Anthropic, Mintlify, FastHTML, and many others. Implementing one is a 30-minute task that pays off as agents and LLM-based search tools mature.</p>
    </div>
